Package: spirula-studio
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3, ffmpeg (>= 10:9.0.2-dmo1+stereo3d14), libstereo-declare1 (>= 1.10), sparky-core-fonts-dialog (>= 1.0), desktop-file-utils, xdg-utils, yad, sparky-aptus-stereo-appcenter (>= 0.1.17), sparky-stereo-apt (>= 20261118.1~sparky9~0), sparky-stereo-graphics, libgl1, libegl1, libxrandr2, libxinerama1, libxcursor1, libxi6, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0
Suggests: spirula-studio-cuda, spirula-studio-model-aliked-n16rot
Description: Build and view 3D models from photos or video
 Spirula Studio reconstructs Gaussian splats and meshes, with a native
 stereo view controlled by Stereo KWin's depth limits. Vulkan is the default.
 Processing model profiles are installed separately from their publishers,
 after their download size and applicable licence terms are shown.
 Purging this package deletes installer-owned downloaded model profiles.

Package: spirula-studio-cuda
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, spirula-studio (= ${binary:Version}), cuda-cudart-13-5
Description: CUDA backend for Spirula Studio
 The same application and features, using CUDA for training on a supported
 NVIDIA GPU. SfM and inference remain available through Vulkan on the GPU
 selected in Graphics. CUDA includes sm_75 and sm_86 code and forward PTX.
 Choose CUDA through the desktop action or --compute-backend cuda.

